But wait: In the above, when SingleStepMode is true, after completing an action we go to ST_IDLE and set stepIndex to next. That means the action command (MoveDown etc.) is still TRUE in the same scan where limit is reached, because we set it at the beginning of the state case. In the next scan, state is ST_IDLE, so output false. That satisfies P03: actionActive & actionLimitReached -> R1(actionCommandOff). Because at the scan where limit reached, action command is still on (actionActive), and next scan it's off. That's fine.

